IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 9 (general provisions): ss 95, 96 and 98.  (ss 89 to 94: deferred; s 97: inert machinery; see COVERAGE.md.)
--
-- FORK 3 (recorded in TV-QUESTION.md section 4; NOTES.md points there): the reach of s 95.  "This Act does not apply to the licensing of any ... broadcasting
-- apparatus under the Broadcasting Act 1994 except ..." can be read two ways.
--   Reading A (the default here): for broadcasting apparatus, the question whether a licence is needed is the
--     Broadcasting Act's alone, so the Telecommunications Act's licensing requirement (the "except in accordance with
--     a licence granted under section 5" of s 54(1) and s 55(1)) does not apply to it.
--   Reading B: s 95 switches off only the Act's licensing machinery (the Authority's power to grant licences) and
--     leaves the offences in ss 54 and 55 as written.
-- "Broadcasting apparatus" is the Broadcasting Act's term (s 2 there: apparatus capable of or designed for the
-- reception of a broadcasting service AND specified in the First Schedule); whether a thing is that is an input here,
-- worked out in the Broadcasting Act's encoding (subjects/sg/broadcasting-act-1994/encodings/legalese-sonnet-5.5/).
-- Stable l4 cannot IMPORT across folders, so there is no code link.

§ `s 95 Excluded matters`

-- src:6987 | 95. This Act does not apply to the licensing of any broadcasting
-- src:6988 | service or any broadcasting apparatus under the Broadcasting
-- src:6989 | Act 1994 except in respect of the regulation of any
-- src:6990 | telecommunication system required for the operation of any
-- src:6991 | broadcasting service or the approval of any broadcasting apparatus
-- src:6992 | used in accordance with section 11.
@ref s 95 (src:6987-6992)
GIVEN `is broadcasting apparatus as the Broadcasting Act 1994 defines it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is the regulation of a telecommunication system required for the operation of a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is the approval of broadcasting apparatus used in accordance with section 11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 95: the Act does not apply to the licensing of this apparatus` MEANS
        `is broadcasting apparatus as the Broadcasting Act 1994 defines it`
    AND (NOT `the question is the regulation of a telecommunication system required for the operation of a broadcasting service`)
    AND (NOT `the question is the approval of broadcasting apparatus used in accordance with section 11`)

§ `s 96 Exemption by Minister`

-- src:7000 | 96. The Minister may exempt any person or class of persons from
-- src:7001 | all or any of the provisions of this Act.
@ref s 96 (src:7000-7001)
GIVEN `the Minister has exempted this person or class of persons from the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 96: the provision does not apply to the person` MEANS
    `the Minister has exempted this person or class of persons from the provision`

§ `s 98 Saving and transitional provisions`

-- src:7088 | 98.—(1) Any scheme, contract, document, licence, permission or
-- src:7089 | resolution prepared, made, granted or approved by the TAS in
-- src:7090 | relation to telecommunication matters under the repealed Act, so far
-- src:7091 | as it is not inconsistent with the provisions of this Act and except as
-- src:7092 | otherwise expressly provided in this Act or in any other written law,
-- src:7093 | continues and is deemed to have been prepared, made, granted or
-- src:7094 | approved by the Authority under the corresponding provisions of this
-- src:7095 | Act.
@ref s 98(1) (src:7088-7095)
GIVEN `granted by TAS in relation to telecommunication matters under the repealed Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is inconsistent with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is otherwise expressly provided in the Act or another written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(1): the scheme, contract, document, licence, permission or resolution continues as the Authority's` MEANS
        `granted by TAS in relation to telecommunication matters under the repealed Act`
    AND (NOT `is inconsistent with the Act`)
    AND (NOT `is otherwise expressly provided in the Act or another written law`)

-- src:7097 | (2) Any subsidiary legislation made under the repealed Act or any
-- src:7098 | other written law relating to telecommunication matters and in force
-- src:7099 | immediately before 1 December 1999, so far as it is not inconsistent
-- src:7100 | with the provisions of this Act, continues in force as if made under
-- src:7101 | this Act until it is revoked or repealed by subsidiary legislation made
-- src:7102 | under this Act.
@ref s 98(2) (src:7097-7102)
GIVEN `subsidiary legislation made under the repealed Act or another written law relating to telecommunication matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in force immediately before 1 December 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is inconsistent with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has been revoked or repealed by subsidiary legislation made under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(2): the subsidiary legislation continues in force as if made under the Act` MEANS
        `subsidiary legislation made under the repealed Act or another written law relating to telecommunication matters`
    AND `in force immediately before 1 December 1999`
    AND (NOT `is inconsistent with the Act`)
    AND (NOT `has been revoked or repealed by subsidiary legislation made under the Act`)
